# OpenEVV sound map: English (Caribbean) (eSpeak NG voice gmw/en-029), spoken by openevv's British English module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template engx
style standard
vowels i I E A a @ c U u H x R e o Y W O I x E x U x Y x W x
glides r l y w
schwa x
secondary 2

# the melody: late; a question that wants yes or no: rise
accent f0=own range=108 shape=2 accent=34 accent2=14 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=14 fe=-12 fq=46 qreg=8 span=2 stressed=88 weak=112 stop=0

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first who what where when why how which whose
whwords first whom

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z

